  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "108",
  "quote": "Neither a landlord nor a tenancy agreement shall require a tenant or prospective tenant to provide post-dated cheques or other negotiable instruments for payment of rent.",
  "reason": "Section 108 explicitly prohibits a tenancy agreement or landlord from requiring a tenant to provide post-dated cheques for rent payments. Any clause imposing such a requirement is inconsistent with the Act and void."
}

